---
import PageContainer from '../components/layout/PageContainer.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = false;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LUDWISE"
  description="Transparent PC game store comparison and discovery platform."
  activeNavId="home"
>
  <PageContainer width="reading">
    <h1 class="lw-text-heading-xl">LUDWISE</h1>
    <p class="lw-text-body-lg">Transparent PC game store comparison and discovery platform.</p>

    {
      /* Not a placeholder any more, and it should not read like one. One store
         is connected, a schedule keeps its catalog filled, and /games can be
         searched. What this page must not do is imply the comparison the
         product describes is finished. One store cannot compare anything, and
         how much of it is here depends on how far the schedule has walked. */
    }
    <p class="lw-text-body-md">
      One store is connected so far, and its catalogue fills over days rather than at once. You can
      search what is here; comparing prices across stores needs a second store, which is not
      connected yet.
    </p>
    <p class="lw-text-body-md">
      <a href="/games">Browse games</a>
    </p>
    {
      /* The spaces after each link are explicit. Prettier wraps a long anchor
         as `</a\n>`, which collapses the whitespace that followed it entirely -
         rendering "READMEfor" and giving a screen reader an unpronounceable
         token. A literal expression survives reformatting. A space in the
         source does not.

         These point at this repository rather than at the backend's own
         documents. The interface is public and its README describes what a
         reader is looking at. The catalog logic is not, and linking to a
         private repository from a public page produces a 404 for everyone
         except the handful of people who can already read it. */
    }
    <p class="lw-text-body-md">
      See <a href="https://github.com/ludwise/ludwise-web">the source</a>{' '}
      for how this interface is built, and{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/ludwise/ludwise-web/blob/main/docs/architecture.md">
        the architecture notes
      </a>{' '}
      for how it reaches the catalogue.
    </p>
  </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
  }

  p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
